  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/86aac25c634d29639329ae53209141ce81a3a82a70d42a4c2dfc6d356ee378b8.png)\n\nIn figure $ABCD$ shown above, which of the following are equal to the vector $\\overset{\\to }{DB}?$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{DA}+\\overset{\\to }{AC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{DA}+\\overset{\\to }{AB}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{BA}-\\overset{\\to }{CA}+\\overset{\\to }{CD}$",
  "worked_solution": "- For the $1$st expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DA}+\\overset{\\to }{AC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB} & =(\\overset{\\to }{DA}+\\overset{\\to }{AC})+\\overset{\\to }{CB} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{DC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{DB}\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the $2$nd expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DA}+\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =\\overset{\\to }{DB}\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the $3$rd expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{BA}-\\overset{\\to }{CA}+\\overset{\\to }{CD} & =(\\overset{\\to }{BA}-\\overset{\\to }{CA})+\\overset{\\to }{CD} \\\\  & =(\\overset{\\to }{BA}+\\overset{\\to }{AC})+\\overset{\\to }{CD} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BC}+\\overset{\\to }{CD} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BD} \\\\  & \\ne \\overset{\\to }{DB}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\".",
